<article class="env-definition" id="07GU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07GU">Definition <span data-tag="07GU">23.3.1</span>.</a> A <em>divided power ring</em> is a triple $(A, I, \gamma )$ where $A$ is a ring, $I \subset A$ is an ideal, and $\gamma = (\gamma _ n)_{n \geq 1}$ is a divided power structure on $I$. A <em>homomorphism of divided power rings</em> $\varphi : (A, I, \gamma ) \to (B, J, \delta )$ is a ring homomorphism $\varphi : A \to B$ such that $\varphi (I) \subset J$ and such that $\delta _ n(\varphi (x)) = \varphi (\gamma _ n(x))$ for all $x \in I$ and $n \geq 1$. </p>
</article>